          "wrong": "어리었을 때 …",
          "right": "어렸을 때 …",
          "why_uz": "어리다 + 었 → 어렸.",
          "why_en": "어리다 + 었 → 어렸."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "한국에 왔을 때에서 …",
          "right": "한국에 왔을 때 …",
          "why_uz": "때 dan keyin 에서 qo'yilmaydi.",
          "why_en": "때 doesn't take 에서."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "고등학생았을 때 …",
          "right": "고등학생이었을 때 …",
          "why_uz": "Ot: N이었을 때.",
          "why_en": "Noun: N이었을 때."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchadagi '-ganda' ga juda mos: 'kelGANIMDA' = 왔을 때, 'kichikLIGIMDA' = 어렸을 때.",
      "compare_en": "Like English 'when' + past: 'WHEN I came' = 왔을 때, 'when I was young' = 어렸을 때 — the 때 ('time') goes after the verb."
    },
    {
      "id": "b3_u03_l2_g2",
      "pattern": "A-(으)ㄴ데, V-는데, N인데 (fon)",
      "meaning_uz": "..., ... (vaziyatni tasvirlab, keyin asosiy gap)",
      "meaning_en": "… and / but … (giving background)",
      "explanation_md": "**-는데** gapning birinchi qismida **fon, vaziyat**ni beradi, ikkinchi qismda esa asosiy fikr keladi. O'zbekchada ko'pincha shunchaki vergul yoki \"..., ...\" bilan beriladi.\n\n**뮤지컬을 봤는데 정말 재미있었어요.** — *Myuzikl ko'rdim, juda qiziq bo'ldi.*  \n**대학로에 갔는데 사람이 많았어요.** — *Teharoga bordim, odam ko'p ekan.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- **Fe'l** → **-는데**: 가다 → **가는데**, 먹다 → **먹는데**\n- **Sifat** → **-(으)ㄴ데**: 비싸다 → **비싼데**, 많다 → **많은데**\n- **Ot** → **N인데**: 학생 → **학생인데**\n- **O'tgan zamon** — hammasida **-았/었는데**: **봤는데**, **비쌌는데**\n- **있다/없다** → **-는데**: 재미있는데, 맛없는데\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Ba'zan **qarama-qarshilik** ham beradi: **기대했는데 실망했어요.** — *Kutgandim, lekin hafsalam pir bo'ldi.*\n- **ㄹ** tushadi: 살다 → **사는데**, 멀다 → **먼데**",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-는데** sets up **background or a situation** in the first half; the main point comes in the second. In English it's often just \"and\" or \"so\".\n\n**뮤지컬을 봤는데 정말 재미있었어요.** — *I saw a musical, and it was really fun.*  \n**대학로에 갔는데 사람이 많았어요.** — *I went to Daehak-ro, and it was crowded.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- **Verb** → **-는데**: 가다 → **가는데**, 먹다 → **먹는데**\n- **Adjective** → **-(으)ㄴ데**: 비싸다 → **비싼데**, 많다 → **많은데**\n- **Noun** → **N인데**: 학생 → **학생인데**\n- **Past** for all: **-았/었는데**: **봤는데**, **비쌌는데**\n- **있다/없다** → **-는데**: 재미있는데, 맛없는데\n\n### Remember\n\n- It can also show **contrast**: **기대했는데 실망했어요.** — *I had high hopes, but I was disappointed.*\n- **ㄹ** drops: 살다 → **사는데**, 멀다 → **먼데**",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l",
          "condition_en": "Verb",
          "rule": "V + 는데",
          "example": "가는데, 먹는데"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Sifat",
          "condition_en": "Adjective",
          "rule": "A + (으)ㄴ데",
          "example": "비싼데, 많은데"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ot",
          "condition_en": "Noun",
          "rule": "N + 인데",
          "example": "학생인데, 주말인데"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "O'tgan",
          "condition_en": "Past",
          "rule": "-았/었는데",
          "example": "봤는데, 비쌌는데"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "뮤지컬을 봤는데 정말 재미있었어요.",
          "uz": "Myuzikl ko'rdim, juda qiziq bo'ldi.",
          "en": "I saw a musical, and it was really fun.",
          "audio": "129fcb328496.mp3"
